1 NOTE Bonaparte, Louis (1778-1846), younger brother of Napoleon, born in 
2 CONT Ajaccio, Corsica, and educated at the military school at 
2 CONT Châlons-sur-Marne, France. He served with his brother in the Italian 
2 CONT campaign of 1796-97 and in Egypt in 1798-99. Napoleon named him king of 
2 CONT Holland in 1806. When Louis disagreed with his policies, Napoleon 
2 CONT dispatched troops against Holland. Louis abdicated in 1810 and lived most 
2 CONT of the remainder of his life in Italy. In 1802 Napoleon arranged the 
2 CONT marriage of Louis and Hortense de Beauharnais (1783-1837), daughter of 
2 CONT Joséphine de Beauharnais and stepdaughter of Napoleon. A son of Louis and 
2 CONT Hortense, Charles Louis Napoleon, became Emperor Napoleon III.
1 NOTE OR "LUIGI"; MADE KING OF HOLLAND BY NAPOLEAN I 1806 (ABDICATED 1810)
