2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Patterson Bonaparte''' (Baltimore, Maryland, 6 February 1785 - Baltimore, Maryland, 4 April 1879), known as "Betsy", was the daughter of a Baltimore, Maryland merchant, and was the first wife of Jérôme Bonaparte, and 
2 CONC sister-in-law of Emperor Napoleon I of France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Emperor annulled the marriage in 1805.
