1 OCCU Prince de Ponte Corvo, Svensk-Norsk kung 1818-1844 - I Norge kallad Karl III Johan, General.adopted by King of Sweden, King of Sweden, King of Norway and Sweden, Roi de Suède, Rey de Suecia y Noruega
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k734069.image.r=jean-baptiste-jules-bernadotte.f64.hl#
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_XIV_Jean
2 CONT https://openplaques.org/people/6175
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first monarch of the Bernadotte dynasty. Born in Pau in southern France, Bernadotte joined the French Royal Army in 1780. Following the outbreak of the French Revolution, he exhibited great military talent, rapidly risi
2 CONC ng through the ranks, and was made a brigadier general by 1794. He served with distinction in Italy and Germany, and was briefly Minister of War. His relationship with Napoleon was turbulent; nevertheless, Napoleon named him a Mar
2 CONC shal of the Empire on the proclamation of the French Empire. Bernadotte played a significant role in the French victory at Austerlitz, and was made Prince of Pontecorvo as a reward. Bernadotte was, through marriage to Désirée Clar
2 CONC y, brother-in-law to Joseph Bonaparte, and thus a member of the extended Imperial family. In 1810, Bernadotte was unexpectedly elected the heir-presumptive (Crown Prince) to the childless King Charles XIII of Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/Sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=12359
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Carl XIV & III Johan''' (26 January 1763 – 8 March 1844) was King of Sweden (as Carl XIV Johan) and King of Norway (as Karl III Johan) from 1818 until his death. Before he became king, he was also the Sovereign Prince of Pontec
2 CONC orvo, in Southern Italy, between 1806 and 1810. ([http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_XIV_of_Sweden Wikipedia] (English))
2 CONT
2 CONT == Name ==
2 CONT
2 CONT "Carl XIV Johan's only baptismal name was, as Fredrik Ulrik Wrangel found out in 1889, "Jean Bernadotte". But that was also the baptismal name of his elder brother. Thus the eldest brother was called Jean-Évangeliste, the younger 
2 CONC Jean-Baptiste. This was apparently not uncommon in Navarre at the time. He always signed "J. Bernadotte". But as a revolutionary general he added a Roman name ("Jules"), which was again not uncommon at the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the Act of Succession of 1810 he is called "Johan Baptist Julius", which is the Swedish version of Jean Baptiste Jules. This was thus his official name during his first months as Crown Prince, and he might have reigned as Joha
2 CONC n IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT "However, when he was adopted by Carl XIII on 2 November 1810 (an act of goodwill which had no constitutional implications) he chose to honour his adoptive father by taking his name, and thus became Carl Johan, dropping Baptist Ju
2 CONC lius."
2 CONT
2 CONT - [http://www.trondni.blogspot.com/2012/02/princess-estelle-silvia-eva-mary.html Trond Norén Isaksen], Feb. 24, 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other summaries ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Name/title: Jean Baptiste Jules Bernadotte
2 CONT
2 CONT Crown Prince of Sweden in 1810.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Carl XIV of Sweden in 1818.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Carl XIV of Norway in 1818.
2 CONT
2 CONT First king of Sweden in the Bernadotte branch
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://www.thepeerage.com/p10226.htm#i102257 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/W/per_page.php?id=5307 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GScid=1969249&GRid=7814605& Find a Grave]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_XIV_John_of_Sweden Wikipedia]
2 CONT *'''King of Sweden and Norway:''' Reign 5 February 1818 – 8 March 1844 
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/310876642120006420 Charles XIII] '''Successor:''' [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000001561849052 Oscar I]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Jean Bapiste Bernadotte var Advokatson från Pau. Mycket ansedd fältherre och administratör, marskalk och fürste av Ponte Corvo under Napoleon Bonaparte, som han dog blev osams med 1809.
2 CONT * Gift 1798 med Désirée Clay, köpmandotter från Marseille, som var svägerska til Napoleon bror, Joseph. Hon hade tidigare varit f¨rlovad med Napoleon.
2 CONT * Den unge löjtnanten, friherre Carl Otto Mörner, tilfrågade på eget initiativ marskalken om han ville bli Sveriges tronfölgere och vid riksdagen i Örebro utsågs han till Kronprins.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT =====Biography of [https://www.geni.com/people/Benjamin-Bloomfield-Baron-Bloomfield-of-Oakhampton-and-Redwood/6000000002263873527 Sir Benjamin Bloomfield]=====
2 CONT
2 CONT Bloomfield was served in Sweden as Envoy- Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary at the Court of Bernadotte, King of Sweden from 1826 - 1831. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The memoirs below are principally posthumous compilations of diaries and letters by Bloomfield while he was appointed as Minister to Sweden. It includes comprehensive and thoughtfully edited letters to his wife, Harriott while pos
2 CONC ted in Sweden, in the Court of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Bernadotte King Charles John] ''(Swedish: Karl Johan)''  known as Bernadotte, titled as King Carl XIV Johan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''[https://archive.org/details/memoirofbenjamin01bloo/ Memoir of Benjamin, Lord Bloomfield, G.C.B., G.C.H, Vol I]'', edited by [https://www.geni.com/people/Georgiana-Lady-Bloomfield/6000000029695810946 Georgiana, Lady Bloomfield
2 CONC ], memoirs of her father-in-law (1884).
2 CONT # ''[https://archive.org/details/memoirofbenjamin02bloo Memoir of Benjamin, Lord Bloomfield, G.C.B., G.C.H, Vol II]'', edited by Georgiana, Lady Bloomfield, memoirs of her father-in-law (1884).
2 CONT
2 CONT ''C'est le 8 de ce mois, à trois heures et demie de l'après - midi qu'est mort Bernadotte, roi de Suède, sous le nom de Charles - Jean XIV. Il était âgé de 81 ans, un mois et douze jours. Il avait régné 36 ans. Son fils est monté 
2 CONC sur le trône sous le nom d'Oscar Ier. Oscar Ier est âgé de 44 ans et demi. Il a de son mariage avec la princesse Joséphine - Maximilienne- Eugénie, fille du prince Eugène Beauharnais, duc de Leuchtenberg, quatre fils et une fille.
2 CONC  Le nouveau prince royal est âgé de 18 ans.''
2 CONT Source : Gazette de Metz du 26 mars 1844  •  Metz, Moselle, Grand Est, France
