1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Virginia Oldoini, Countess of Castiglione''' (22 March 1837 – 28 November 1899), better known as La Castiglione, was an Italian courtesan who achieved notoriety as a mistress of Emperor Napoleon III of France. S
2 CONC he was also a significant figure in the early history of photography.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1871, just after the defeat of France in the Franco-Prussian War, she was called to a secret meeting with Otto von Bismarck to explain to him how the German occupation of Paris could be fatal to his interests. She may have been
2 CONC  persuasive, as Paris was spared Prussian occupation.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Links ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_Oldoini Wiki - Virginia Oldoini]
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Interesting article about her life: https://www.lastampa.it/torino/appuntamenti/2012/01/14/news/il-taccuino-proibito-della-contessa-1.36506135/ 
2 CONT
2 CONT -Added 11 Nov, 2024 K. Welborn
