1 NOTE !MAR - BETSY BONAPARTE, THE BELLE OF BALTIMORE by Claude Bourguignon-Frasseto, p. 4
2 CONT In 1778, when he (William Patterson) returned to Philadelphia, he was rich and enjoyed great favor with the Congress with the commanding general.  He bought some real estate in the deviloping market town of Baltimore and elsewhere
2 CONC  in Maryland and then decided to get married:  his bride was pretty Dorcas Spear, daughter of a local notable.  They settled in Baltimore.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid, p. 114
2 CONT This last blow saps the last of Dorcas's strength:  she will gently pass away during the winter (because of their son Octavius being killed in the War of 1812, really in 1814.)
