1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Count Alfred Émilien O'Hara van Nieuwerkerke (16 April 1811, Paris - 16 January 1892, Gattaiola, near Lucca) was a French sculptor of Dutch descent (his grandfather was the illegitimate son of a minor stadholder) a
2 CONC nd a high-level civil servant in the Second French Empire. He is also notable as the lover of Mathilde Bonaparte, after her estrangement from her husband Anatole Demidov.
2 CONT
