1 NOTE He became an admiral of the Austrian navy and governor from 1857 to 1859 
2 CONT of the Lombardo-Venetian territory. In 1863 the French emperor Napoleon 
2 CONT III persuaded Maximilian to accept the crown of Mexico. Believing that 
2 CONT they had the support of the people, he and his wife went to Mexico in 
2 CONT 1864. Backed by French troops, they were installed as the country's rulers 
2 CONT over the opposition of the republicans. After 1865, the United States, 
2 CONT which objected to France's intervention but had been distracted by its own 
2 CONT civil war, began pressuring the French to pull out. When they did withdraw 
2 CONT in 1867, Maximilian refused to go with them. After that, republican forces 
2 CONT under Benito Juárez quickly regained control of Mexico. Captured by the 
2 CONT republicans at Querétaro, Maximilian was tried by court-martial and shot.
