1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Through his marriage to Charlotte Jane Windsor, the estates of the Herberts, Earls of Pembroke, afterwards descended to the house of Bute."
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft#page/306/mode/2up<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Crichton-Stuart,_1st_Marquess_of_Bute
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stuart, 1st Marquess of Bute PC, FRS''' (30 June 1744 – 16 November 1814), styled Lord Mount Stuart until 1792 and known as The Earl of Bute between 1792 and 1794, was a British nobleman.<br/>
2 CONT <br/>He was the son of '''John Stuart, 3rd Earl of Bute''' and the former '''Mary Wortley Montagu''', a granddaughter of the 1st Duke of Kingston-upon-Hull and great-granddaughter of the 1st Earl of Sandwich. He was educated at Wi
2 CONC nchester and Oxford University, and around 1757 he began to be tutored by the later famous Scottish philosopher Adam Ferguson<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord Bute''' married the '''Honourable Charlotte Hickman-Windsor''', daughter of Herbert Hickman-Windsor, 2nd Viscount Windsor, on 12 November 1766. They had several children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * John Stuart, Lord Mount Stuart (25 September 1767 – 22 January 1794), whose son succeeded as 2nd Marquess
2 CONT * Lord Evelyn Stuart (1773–1842), a colonel in the army
2 CONT * Lady Charlotte Stuart (c. 1775 – 5 September 1847), married Sir William Homan, 1st Baronet
2 CONT * Lord Henry Stuart (7 June 1777 – 19 August 1809), father of Henry Villiers-Stuart, 1st Baron Stuart de Decies
2 CONT * Captain Lord William Stuart (18 November 1778 – 28 July 1814)
2 CONT * Rear-Admiral Lord George Stuart (1 March 1780 – 19 February 1841 )
2 CONT His first wife died on 28 January 1800. He married '''Frances Coutts''', daughter of Thomas Coutts, on 17 September 1800. They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Lady Frances Stuart (d. 29 March 1859)
2 CONT * Lord Dudley Coutts Stuart (11 January 1803 – 17 November 1854)
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife outlived him, and died on 12 November 1832.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [http://thepeerage.com/p11243.htm#i112426 The Peerage] 112426
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''John Stuart, 1st Marquess of the County of Bute''' 
2 CONT * Born on 30 June 1744 at Mount Stuart, Rothesay, Isle of Bute, Scotland.
2 CONT * Son of John Stuart, 3rd Earl of Bute and Mary Wortley-Montagu, Baroness Mount Stuart of Wortley.
2 CONT * Married, '''firstly''', - '''Hon. Charlotte Jane Windsor''', daughter of Herbert Hickman-Windsor, 2nd Viscount Windsor of Blackcastle and Alice Clavering, on 12 November 1766 at St. John's Chapel, St. George Hanover Square, Lond
2 CONC on, England.
2 CONT * Married, '''secondly''' -, '''Frances Coutts''', daughter of Thomas Coutts and Susan Starkie, on 17 September 1800 at Stratton Street, St. George Hanover Square, London, England.
2 CONT * Died on 16 November 1814 at age 70 at Geneva, Switzerland.
2 CONT * Educated at 
2 CONT >* Winchester College, Winchester, Hampshire, England.
2 CONT >* Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England. 
2 CONT * Held the office of 
2 CONT >* Member of Parliament (M.P.) (Tory) for Bossiney between 1766 and 1776.
2 CONT >* Lord-Lieutenant of Glamorganshire between 1772 and 1793.<br/>
2 CONT >* Auditor of the Imprest between 1781 and 1782
2 CONT >* Ambassador to Spain between March 1783 and December 1783<br/>
2 CONT >* Lord-Lieutenant of Bute between 1794 and 1814.
2 CONT >* Lord-Lieutenant of Glamorganshire between 1794 and 1814.<br/>
2 CONT >* Ambassador to Spain between 1795 and 1796<br/>
2 CONT >* Counsellor of State [Scotland] to the Prince of Wales in 1806.
2 CONT * Created 1st Baron Cardiff of Cardiff Castle [Great Britain] on 20 May 1776, in recognition of his vast South Wales properties.
2 CONT * Invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) in 1779.1
2 CONT * Envoy to Turin between 1779 and 1783.
2 CONT * Styled as Viscount Mount Stuart in 1783.
2 CONT * Succeeded to the title
2 CONT >* 4th Lord Mountstuart, Cumra and Inchmarnock [S., 1703] on 10 March 1792.
2 CONT >* 6th Baronet Stuart, of Bute [N.S., 1627] on 10 March 1792.
2 CONT >* 4th Earl of Bute [S., 1703] on 10 March 1792.
2 CONT >* 4th Viscount Kingarth [S., 1703] on 10 March 1792.
2 CONT >* 2nd Baron Mount Stuart of Wortley, co. York [G.B., 1761] on 6 November 1794.
2 CONT * Created 
2 CONT >* 1st Earl of Windsor [Great Britain] on 27 February 1796.
2 CONT >* 1st Marquess of the County of Bute [Great Britain] on 27 February 1796.
2 CONT >* 1st Viscount Mountjoy, of the Isle of Wight [Great Britain] on 27 February 1796, commemorating his first wife's parentage.
2 CONT * Invested as a Fellow, Royal Society (F.R.S.) on 12 December 1799.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of John Stuart, 1st Marquess of the County of Bute and Hon. Charlotte Jane Windsor'''
2 CONT * John Stuart, Viscount Mount Stuart b. 25 Sep 1767, d. 22 Jan 1794
2 CONT * Lady Charlotte Stuart b. c 1775, d. 5 Sep 1847
2 CONT * Lt. Lord Charles Stuart b. 18 Jul 1775, d. 11 Feb 1796
2 CONT * Lord Henry Stuart b. 7 Jun 1777, d. 19 Aug 1809
2 CONT * Captain Lord William Stuart b. 18 Nov 1778, d. 28 Jul 1814
2 CONT * Rear-Admiral Lord George Stuart b. 1 Mar 1780, d. 19 Feb 1841
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of John Stuart, 1st Marquess of the County of Bute and Frances Coutts'''
2 CONT * Lady Frances Stuart d. 29 Mar 1859
2 CONT * Lord Dudley Coutts Stuart b. 11 Jan 1803, d. 17 Nov 1854<br/>
2 CONT <span>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
