1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The 20 year difference between his birth and that of his last born sibling suggests an inaccuracy.
2 CONT For the moment we are obliged to follow the info on his baptism which is the only recorded evidence of him.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has no known birth registration but his baptism coincides with his Sister's relationship with Napoleon III . 	Baptised at The Chapel Royal Brighton 13 Jan 1847 as the son of his sister's parents
2 CONT
2 CONT ***Added screenshot/crop of baptism records from Brighton. His possible maternal grandparents Elizabeth & Joseph appear as his parents. See sources. Karrie Anderson Welborn,  
2 CONT
2 CONT No trace of a William Alderton Haryett post his Brighton baptism in 1847. The address (15 North Street, Brighton) given at his baptism was that of his baptismal father Joseph’s brother in law, Charles Alderton (a tailor) and his w
2 CONC ife Frances nee Haryett.  In 1851, his sister's son Martin (fathered by Capt Mountjoy) was also at that address.
2 CONT
2 CONT Could these be his birth and death?
2 CONT Births Dec 1846  Alderton	 William	 	 Bury St Edmunds	 13	399	
2 CONT Deaths Sep 1848  Alderton	 William	  	 Bury St Eds	 13	256	  
