1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/41659425/jerome-napoleon_charles-bonaparte
2 CONT
2 CONT Having inherited a fortune, Jerome Napoleon Charles Bonaparte never had a job or practiced a profession. He ended his rather useless existence in Central Park. Walking his wife's dog he stumbled over its leash and broke his neck.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Jerome Napoleon Charles Bonaparte was born on 26 February 1878, in Paris, Seine, France, his father, Jerome Napoleon Bonaparte, was 47 and his mother, Caroline Le Roy Appleton “Madame Bonaparte”, was 37. He married Blanche Pi
2 CONC erce Pierce on 8 April 1914, in Manhattan, New York City, New York, United States. He died on 10 November 1945, in Manhattan, New York City, New York, United States, at the age of 67, and was buried in Loudon Park Cemetery, Baltim
2 CONC ore, Maryland, United States.
