2 CONT He was shown as a son Thomas in the will of Thomas Savage, Gent., of Cherry Stones. He was given, after term of 21 years, the land in N'hamp whereon Negro Daniel Webb now lives. He was also given the 700 acre plantation whereon Jo
2 CONC hn Lowry now lives adjoining Webb. When his father's will was probated it was noted that his brother George, who was named Extr. in his father's will, was dec'd and Thomas Savage, the son and heir-at-law, objected to the devise of
2 CONC  land in the will and qualified to settle his father's estate.
