1 TITL Count
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1870 Count Napoleon Ledochowski, a great pianist and teacher, came to Chicago and founded a conservatory of music. Count Ledochowski was the son of Count Constantine and the grandson of Baron de Meneval, secreta
2 CONC ry to Napoleon. He graduated from the Sorbonne University, where he studied music under the instruction of one of Chopin's pupils. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Ledochowski was most highly gifted as he was an able painter, as well as a capable musician. His paintings were exhibited at the Exposition Art Hall. He was an excellent singer as evidenced by the fact that the Apollo Musica
2 CONC l Club of Chicago, the oldest choral group in the Middle West, comparable with the Chicago Symphony Orchestra in making history for Chicago, engaged him as a soloist for a number of their concerts. Surely, a gentleman, possessing 
2 CONC the artistic culture such as that of Count Ledochowski, was able to impart a genuine and very productive musical training to the scores of young Chicagoans who were fortunate enough to come under his tutelage.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/polesofchicago1800zgle/polesofchicago1800zgle_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''OBITUARY'''
2 CONT
2 CONT LEDOCHOWSKI, POLISH COUNT, DIES IN CHICAGO
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Napoleon Ledochowski died yesterday at his residence, 3512 Lake Park avenue. He was 72 years old and had been a resident of Chicago for forty-nine years. Count Ledochowski was an artist and at one time was considered the bes
2 CONC t pianist in Chicago.
2 CONT
2 CONT His grandfather was Baron de Menedal, who went as private secretary with Napoleon to St. Helena. Count Ledochowski's father went to Paris at the time of the partition of Poland , and married a daughter of Baron de Menedal. It was 
2 CONC in Paris that Count Ledochowski was born. His brother, a brigadier general in the French army, died about a year ago. He is a cousin of Father Wladimir Ledochowski, general of the Society of Jesus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Ledochowski was a bachelor. Funeral service will be held tomorrow morning at Holy Angels church. Burial will be at Graceland.
