2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Princess Luisa Carlotta of the Two Sicilies
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Luisa Carlotta of Bourbon (October 24, 1804 – January 29, 1844), Princess the Two Sicilies, Infanta of Spain, was a daughter of King Francis I of the Two Sicilies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Luisa Carlotta was born at Portici, the eldest child of King Francis I and of his wife Infanta Maria Isabella of Spain. Her maternal grandfather was King Charles IV of Spain. Luisa Carlotta had eleven younger brothers and sisters,
2 CONC  including King Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 12, 1819 in Madrid, Luisa Carlotta married her maternal uncle Infante Francisco de Paula of Spain. He was ten years older than Luisa Carlotta. They had eleven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Francisco de Asís (1820-1821), died young
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella (1821-1897)
2 CONT
2 CONT Francisco de Asís (1822-1902), married Queen Isabella II of Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT Enrique Maria Fernando (1823-1870)
2 CONT
2 CONT Louisa (1824-1900)
2 CONT
2 CONT Duarte Felipe (1826-1830), died young
2 CONT
2 CONT Josefina (1827-1920)
2 CONT
2 CONT Theresa (1828-1829), died young
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernando (1832-1854)
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Christina (1833-1902), married Sebastian Gabriël de Bourbon, great-grandson of King Charles III of Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT Amelia (1834-1905), married Prince Adalbert of Bavaria, youngest son of King Ludwig I of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Luisa Carlotta died at Madrid at the age of 39.
