2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p11442.htm#i114411
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Theresa Christina Maria of Bourbon-Two Sicilies; 14 March 1822 - 28 December 1889) was the empress consort of Pedro II of Brazil and Princess of the Two Sicilies. She was the daughter of King Francis I of the Two Sicilies and Mari
2 CONC a Isabella of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Empress Teresa suffered from a cardiac arrest a few days after the military coup of 15 November 1889. During the journey of the Imperial Family to exile, Teresa was horrified by the rude treatment of the republicans dedicated to d
2 CONC estroying the dynasty. To the ambassador of Austria she said that, "we are treated as criminals". On landing in Portugal she left for a simple hotel, in the city of the Porto, where she became ill. A doctor was called in and said 
2 CONC nothing could be done. She was buried in the Pantheon of São Vicente de Fora, from where her remains have been transferred to the Imperial Mausoleum of the Cathedral of Petrópolis.
