1 NOTE He was a patron of literature and the arts and traveled extensively. He 
2 CONT wrote about his travels in Travels in the East (1884; translated 1884).  
2 CONT His romantic attachment with a young Austrian noblewoman, Baroness Marie 
2 CONT Vetsera (1871-89), ended in the violent death of both. Their bodies were 
2 CONT found in a hunting lodge at Mayerling, near Vienna. Although the Austrian 
2 CONT government officially announced that the lovers had committed suicide, 
2 CONT unsubstantiated rumors of foul play have persisted to the present day, 
2 CONT chiefly because of the archduke's sympathy with the cause of Hungarian 
2 CONT nationalism.
