1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nazareno_Strampelli
2 CONT
2 CONT Nazareno Strampelli (May 29, 1866 in Castelraimondo, Italy – January 23, 1942) was an Italian agronomist and plant breeder. He was the forerunner of what became known as the Green Revolution of the late 1960s. Strampelli's work al
2 CONC lowed Italy to become almost self-sufficient in bread wheat production, relative to Italy's contemporaneous population and consumption patterns, increasing area-based agricultural intensity from an average yield of 1.0 t/ha at the
2 CONC  beginning of the 19th century to about 1.5 t/ha in the 1930s,[1] through the hybridization of wheat into high-yield varietals.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
