1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Stuart,_Lord_Mount_Stuart
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stuart, Lord Mount Stuart (25 September 1767 – 22 January 1794), was an England-born Scottish Tory politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mount Stuart was the son of the John Stuart, 1st Marquess of Bute and the grandson of Prime Minister John Stuart, 3rd Earl of Bute. His mother was the Hon. Charlotte Jane, daughter and heiress of Herbert Windsor, 2nd Viscount Wind
2 CONC sor. He was born at Grosvenor Square, London in 1767 and educated at Eton and St John's College, Cambridge.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1790, he was elected Member of Parliament for Cardiff, a seat he held until his death. He was appointed Colonel of the Glamorganshire Militia in 1791 and was also Lord-Lieutenant of Glamorganshire between 1793 and his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Mount Stuart married Lady Elizabeth McDouall-Crichton, daughter of Patrick McDouall-Crichton, 6th Earl of Dumfries, and his wife Margaret (née Crauford), on 12 October 1792. They had two sons, who both added the surname "Cric
2 CONC hton" before that of "Stuart" in 1805:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Crichton-Stuart, 2nd Marquess of Bute (10 August 1793 – 18 March 1848)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Patrick James Herbert Crichton-Stuart (25 August 1794 – 7 September 1859). In 1817 he obtained the rank of the son of a Marquess, which his father would have been, had he not died before his father, the 1st Marquess.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Mount Stuart died at Bassingbourn Hall near Stansted, Essex, in January 1794, only 26 years of age, a month after being injured in a fall from his horse. Lady Mount Stuart survived him by three years and died in July 1797, ag
2 CONC ed 24.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://thepeerage.com/p2390.htm#i23895 The Peerage]<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stuart, Viscount Mount Stuart''' 
2 CONT * Born on 25 September 1767 at Grosvenor Square, Mayfair, London, England.
2 CONT * Son of John Stuart, 1st Marquess of the County of Bute and Hon. Charlotte Jane Windsor.1 
2 CONT * Married '''Lady Elizabeth Penelope MacDowall-Crichton''', daughter of Patrick MacDowall-Crichton, 6th Earl of Dumfries and Margaret Crauford, on 12 October 1792 at Dumfries House, Cumnock, Ayrshire, Scotland.
2 CONT * Died on 22 January 1794 at age 26 at Bassingbourn Hall, England, from a fall from his horse.
2 CONT * Buried at Stanton Rivers, Essex, England.
2 CONT * Died intestate and his estate was administered in February 1794.
2 CONT * Educated between 1775 and 1779 at Eton College, Windsor, Berkshire, England.
2 CONT * Matriculated at St. John's College, Cambridge University, Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England, on 27 May 1784.
2 CONT * Graduated from St. John's College, Cambridge University, Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England, in 1787 with a Master of Arts (M.A.).
2 CONT * Held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) (Tory) for Cardiff between 1790 and 1794.
2 CONT * Styled as Viscount Mount Stuart between 1792 and 1794, incorrectly.
2 CONT * Held the office of Lord-Lieutenant of Glamorganshire between 1793 and 1794.
2 CONT ===Children of John Stuart, Viscount Mount Stuart and Lady Elizabeth Penelope MacDowall-Crichton<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT * John Crichton-Stuart, 2nd Marquess of the County of Bute b. 10 Aug 1793, d. 18 Mar 1848
2 CONT * Lord Patrick James Herbert Crichton-Stuart b. 25 Aug 1794, d. 7 Sep 1859<br/>
2 CONT <span>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
