1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sidonie-Gabrielle Colette (French: [kɔ.lɛt]; 28 January 1873 – 3 August 1954), known mononymously as Colette, was a French author and woman of letters. She was nominated for the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1948, a
2 CONC nd was also known as a mime, actress, and journalist. Colette is best remembered for her 1944 novella Gigi, which was the basis for the 1958 film and the 1973 stage production of the same name.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colette
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colette Colette], de son vrai nom Sidonie-Gabrielle Colette, est une romancière française, née à Saint-Sauveur-en-Puisaye (Yonne) le 28 janvier 1873, morte à Paris le 3 août 1954. Elle est élue memb
2 CONC re de l’Académie Goncourt en 1945.
2 CONT * Colette was the surname of the French novelist Sidonie-Gabrielle Colette (28 January 1873 – 3 August 1954). She is best known for her novel Gigi (upon which the stage and film musical comedies by Lerner & Loewe, of the same titl
2 CONC e, were based). http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colette
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *http://www.libros.am/book/read/id/344866/slug/coco-chanel-an-intimate-life
