2 CONC w that the weapon existed at alL Miss Virginia Lewis, .th- owner of it, always kept it so quiet that very -few of us realized" that the distinguished article was preserved. When you consider, what George Washington was to us and w
2 CONC hat his sword was to him, it becomes apparent that of all the heirlooms preserved in America this is the most important. No wonder that Miss Lewis refused $50,000 for it and chooses to hold out for $100,000.  ...  "The said Samuel
