1 TITL Maj.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Major George Lewis died at his seat at Marmion in King George county, Va., in 1821
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 46. Major George Lewis, Captain of Washington's Life Guard, married Catherine Daingerfield, of "Coventry", in Spotsylvania, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Samuel Lewis, born November 11, 1780, who had ALLOWAY LEWIS, HENRY HOWELL LEWIS, late of Baltimore, MARY LEWIS, married John Casey, GEORGE, THOMAS, and JOHN LEWIS
2 CONT *2. Mary Willis Lewis, born June 24, 1782, married Major Byrd Charles Willis
2 CONT *3.Daingerfield Lewis, born 14 July, 1785, married Miss Pratt, daughter of Thomas Pratt and Jane Brockenbrough
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA with the rank of CAPTAIN.  DAR Ancestor #:[https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A069946  A069946].
2 CONT
2 CONT Info added per DAR's "Lineage Book of the Charter Members" by Mary S Lockwood and published 1895 stating:
2 CONT
2 CONT Maj George Lewis "commanded Washington's bodyguard in the battle of Princeton."
2 CONT
2 CONT Children listed in DAR record:
2 CONT * Mary
2 CONT * Samuel
2 CONT * Dangerfield
2 CONT
2 CONT North American Family Histories 1500-200 also list daughter Bettie. She is not mentioned in his will. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.revolutionarywararchives.org/lewis.html
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/10128950/george-washington-lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT George Washington Lewis is the Nephew of General George Washington, He served his country on the staff of his uncle during the Revolutionary War. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Fielding and Betty (Washington) Lewis of Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at Kenmore Plantation in Fredericksburg,VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Attended Princeton College
2 CONT
2 CONT REV. WAR: 
2 CONT
2 CONT On March 12th, 1776, Gen. George Washington created the "Commander-in-Chief Guard" appointing Captain Caleb Gibbs Commandant and George Lewis First Lieutenant as second in command (George Lewis was 19)
2 CONT
2 CONT October 15th, 1779, George Washington Lewis married Catherine Daingerfield, daughter of Colonel William Daingerfield, who had been the Commander of the Seventh Virginia Regiment of the Continental Line.
2 CONT
2 CONT When George Washington died, December 14th, 1799, he left land and gave George Lewis first choice of his swords, which was highly prized in the 18th century.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Mar. 13, 1757 Fredericksburg Fredericksburg City Virginia, USA Death: 	Nov. 13, 1821 Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT George Washington Lewis is the Nephew of General George Washington, He served his country on the staff of his uncle during the Revolutionary War. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Fielding and Betty (Washington) Lewis of Virginia/born at Kenmore Plantation in Fredericksburg,VA. Attended Princeton College
2 CONT
2 CONT REV. WAR: March 12th, 1776/Gen. George Washington created the "Commander-in-Chief Guard" appointing Captain Caleb Gibbs Commandant and George Lewis First Lieutenant as second in command(George Lewis was 19)
2 CONT
2 CONT October 15th, 1779/George Washington Lewis married CATHERINE DANGERFIELD/daughter of Colonel William Daingerfield, who had been the Commander of the Seventh Virginia Regiment of the Continental Line.
2 CONT
2 CONT When George Washington died, December 14th, 1799, he left land and gave George Lewis first choice of his swords, which was highly prized in the 18th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT **his wife Catherine Dangerfield Lewis is buried in same cemetery and they could be linked.Memorial# 1370338/Willis Cemetery/Maryes Heights Fredericksburg City Virginia USA 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT At the Battle of Princeton he was aide to General Hugh Mercer who died in his arms, He was attached to the command of cavalry, of the Commander-in-Chief, and was at Brandywine, Germantown and Monmouth. He was mentioned in the will
2 CONC  of George Washington. Source: North America, Family Histories, 1500-2000 for George Lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
