2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT At the Saturday evening of September 24, 1803, in Ludwigslust Palace, Mecklenburg-Schwerin, Her Imperial Highness Grand Duchess Helena Pavlovna died from tuberculosis at age 18.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was granddaughter and goddaughter of Catherine II, daughter of Emperor Paul I and sister of Alexander I.
2 CONT
2 CONT In her 14 Helena was married to His Serene Highness Hereditary Prince Frederick Louis of Mecklenburg whom she bore son Paul Frederick, future Grand Duke of Mecklenburg(-Schwerin), and daughter Marie.
2 CONT
2 CONT When in 1874 Paul Frederick's granddaughter Marie married a son of Russian Emperor, she received the patronymics 'Pavlovna' in memory of her ancestor Emperor Paul.
2 CONT
2 CONT Helena Pavlovna was buried in Schwerin.
