1 NOTE !BIRTH - BALTIMORE CITY DEATHS AND BURIALS 1834-1840 by Henry C. Peden, Jr., p. 335
2 CONT SMITH, Samuel, age 87, d. April 22, 1839 of old age, buried in First Presbyterian (Westminster) Cem.  Was a Lt. Col. in the Revolutionary War, Major General in the War of 1812, Acting U.S. Secretary of the Navy, U.S. Congressman, 
2 CONC U.S. Senator and Mayor of Baltimore.  A native of Lancaster Co., PA, Samuel Smith was born on July 27, 1752, educated in England, served in the Maryland Line, and resided for 79 years in Baltimore.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - DAR PATRIOT INDEX CENTENNIAL EDITION, PART III by NSDAR Centennial Administration p. 2722
2 CONT Samuel Smith was married to Margaret Spear.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE MARYLAND JOURNAL AND THE BALTIMORE ADVERTISER - GLEANINGS FROM MARYLAND NEWSPAPERS 1776-1785 by Robert W. Barnes p. 45
2 CONT SMITH, Col. Samuel and Miss Peggy Spear, daughter of William Spear, Esq. of this town, was married. (MD. Gazette 5 Jan. 1779)
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - See Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid
2 CONT He was buried in First Presbyterian (Westminster) Cem., Section #85
2 CONT Samuel Smith (1752-1839) Merchant, Revolution, War of 1812, Acting U.S. Secretary of the Navy, U.S. Congress, Senate, Mayor
2 CONT Gen'l Samuel Smith B. 1752 d. 1839
