1 NOTE !BIRTH - JOSHUA JOHNSON, FREEMAN AND EARLY AMERICAN PORTRAIT PAINTER by Carolyn J. Weekley, Stiles Tuttle Colwill with Leroy Graham & Mary Ellen Hayward - 1987 , p. 99
2 CONT John Spear Smith (1786-1866) was born in Baltimore and later attended the College of William and Mary in Virginia; he continued his studies at Harvard University.  He was a lawyer in adult life and served as an attache to the Unit
2 CONC ed States Legation in London in 1809-1810.  Smith also served as President of the Maryland Historical Society from 1843 to 1866.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT His wife was Caryanne Nicholas, a daughter of Virginia Governor Wilson Cary Nicholas.
