1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sidney (Turner) Dyer (1857-1933)
2 CONT Daughter of William Fauntleroy Turner (1812-1872) & Sidney (Patterson) Turner (1829-1858)
2 CONT Married Donnell Swan (Divorce) and than Elisha Dyer IV (1862-1917).
2 CONT She was a great-granddaughter of William Patterson, 1st President of the Bank of Maryland and founder of the Baltimore & Ohio Railroad. Her great-aunt, Betsey Patterson, married Jerome-Napoleon Bonaparte, youngest brother of the E
2 CONC mperor Napoleon. Sidney was the mother of one daughter by her first marriage (that ended in divorce), Laura Patterson (Swan) Robeson, but had no children by her second marriage.
