1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=64007578
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Baltimore (Independent City), Maryland, United States - 1806
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/9XSW-22K FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 10 2017, 20:39:36 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1806 Death: 	May 6, 1834
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was the daughter of Nathaniel Morton and Sarah (Copeland) Morton Williams.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary's half-sister was Susan May (Williams) Bonaparte (2 Apr 1812 - 15 Sept 1881). She was the daughter of Benjamin Williams, of Roxbury, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married Hon. David Stewart (13 Sept 1800 - 5 Jan 1858) on 20 Oct 1825 in Baltimore, Maryland, as his first wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT David was born in Baltimore, Maryland, to John Stewart (died Mar c.1802) and Helen (West) Stewart (4 Apr 1777 - 1860).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1838, David built the family homestead, "Upton," at 811 W. Lanvale Street in Baltimore City, Maryland. In 1868, Francis W. Dammann purchased "Upton". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary died of "inflammation of the brain."
2 CONT
2 CONT David [2nd] married Priscilla Margaretta (Pinkney) Stewart (born 5 Aug 1805) on 9 June 1836 in Baltimore, Maryland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Priscilla was the daughter of Jonathan Pinkney and Rebecca (?) Davidson Pinkney (born c.1780).
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1860 U.S. Census, Priscilla was living in Baltimore City, Maryland, with her mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1870 U.S. Census, Priscilla was living with her brother, Capt. Robert Frederick Pinkney (born 13 May 1811), and sister, Henrietta Maria Pinkney (born 17 Sept 1809).
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1880 U.S. Census, Priscilla was living in Baltimore City, Maryland. Her sister, Henrietta, was living with her. _____
2 CONT
2 CONT The other children of David and Adelaide were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) SARAH STEWART died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) JOHN STEWART (27 Feb 1826 - 26 Feb 1901) was born and died in Baltimore, Maryland. He [1st] married Henrietta B. (Gaither) Stewart (1826 - 1850) on 7 Dec 1848 in Baltimore, Maryland. Henrietta is #119820047.
2 CONT
2 CONT John [2nd] married Leonice Josephine (Moulton) Stewart (9 May 1934 - 13 Feb 1922) on 20 Oct 1853 in Troy, New York. She was born in New York to Joseph White Moulton (1789-1875) and Leonice Marsden (Sampson) Moulton (1811-1897). Le
2 CONC onice is #54175864. She is buried in the same cemetery as their daughter, Leonice Moulton (Stewart) Shaw.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Leonice were the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) Helen West (Stewart) Ridgely (27 July 1854 - Apr 1929) was born at "Upton", Baltimore City, Maryland. She married Capt. John Ridgely, Sr. (22 Feb 1851 - 1938) of “Hampton Mansion” on 11 Sept 1873. He was the son of Charles Ridg
2 CONC ely (1830-1872) and Margaretta Sophia (Howard) Ridgely (1824-1904).
2 CONT
2 CONT b) David Stewart (born 24 Oct 1856) was born in Maryland.
2 CONT
2 CONT c) Leonice Moulton (Stewart) Shaw ["Nona"] (22 May 1858 - 29 Jan 1920) married William Checkley Shaw (4 Feb 1852 - 9 Dec 1918) on 20 Feb 1877. He was born in Maryland to William C. Shaw (1824-1874) and Ann (DeButts) Shaw (1831-185
2 CONC 9). William was the brother of Sophia Shaw (born c.1854) and Anna Shaw (born c.1857).
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Sarah Copeland Williams (1778 - 1870)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   David Stewart (1800 - 1858)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Charles Morton Stewart (1828 - 1900)*
2 CONT   David Stewart (1833 - 1834)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sibling:
2 CONT   Mary Adelaide Morton Stewart (1806 - 1834)
2 CONT   Susan May Williams Bonaparte (1812 - 1881)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Westminster Burial Ground  Baltimore Baltimore City Maryland, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Edit Virtual Cemetery info [?]
2 CONT
