1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Blanche Pierce was born to Emily Hill Pierce and Edward Pierce of Newtonville, MA. Emily came from Rochester, NY. Blanche was married twice - first to Harold Strebeigh from New York. They were married about the tur
2 CONC n of the century and divorced in 1914 when she married her second husband, Jerome Napoleon Bonaparte. Blanche had three children by her first husband, Strebeigh -a son who died in childhood and twin daughters - Blanche and Barbara
2 CONC  who lived into their nineties. Blanche and Jerome N. Bonaparte had no children but they had a lot of society. Blanche was a bit of a social climber and she reached the summit after she married Bonaparte.
