0 @N6000000002322348759@ NOTE A rich young army officer who was ashamed of Josephine's provincial manners
1 CONT and lack of sophistication, declined to present her at the court of
1 CONT Marie-Antoinette at Versailles. Separating in March 1785, the French
1 CONT Revolution at hand with her husband then being part of the Revolutionary
1 CONT army, he fell out of favor by left-wing Jacobins and was guillotined in June
1 CONT 1794. Josephine was imprisoned, but the coup d'etat of 9 Thermdor (July 27)
1 CONT ended the Terror and she was released to catch the eye of one Napoleon.
