1 CONT Prince Edward Augustus, Duke of York and Albany From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Prince Edward Augustus, Duke of York (14 March 1739 -17 September 1767) was the younger brother of George III of Great Britain, the second son of Frederick, Prince of Wales and Augusta of Saxe-Gotha. He was created Duke of York an
1 CONC d Albany by his paternal grandfather George II in 1760.
1 CONT
1 CONT Between the death of his paternal grandfather on 25 October 1760 and the birth of George, Prince of Wales on 12 August 1762, he was Heir Presumptive to the British throne.
