1 CONT Prince William Henry, Duke of Gloucester and Edinburgh From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT HRH Prince William Henry, Earl of Connaught, 1st Duke of Gloucester and Edinburgh (November 14, 1743 - August 25, 1805) was a British prince and military officer, younger brother of King George III.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was born to Frederick Louis, Prince of Wales and Augusta of Saxe-Gotha at Leicester House in London. His brother King George III created him Duke of Edinburgh, Duke of Gloucester and Earl of Connaught in 1764.
1 CONT
1 CONT Prince William Henry, Duke of Gloucester was most known for his secret marriage to Maria, Dowager Countess Waldegrave, an illegitimate granddaughter of Sir Robert Walpole. This marriage and that of his brother prompted the passing
1 CONC  of the Royal Marriages Act. The Duke of Gloucester had three children by his wife - 1. Her Highness Princess Sophia of Gloucester (1773-1844) 2. Her Highness Princess Caroline of Gloucester (1774-1775) 3. His Highness Prince Will
1 CONC iam Frederick of Gloucester (1776-1834), m. HRH The Princess Mary, no issue
1 CONT
1 CONT Prince William Henry was appointed (in an honorary fashion) to colonel of the 13th Regiment of Foot, 3rd Regiment of Foot Guards, and 1st Regiment of Foot Guards, and he became a field marshal on October 12, 1793. He died at Glouc
1 CONC ester House in London.
1 CONT
1 CONT Titles His Royal Highness Prince William Henry of Wales (1743-1764) His Royal Highness The Duke of Gloucester (1764-1805)
0 @N6000000007329600893@ NOTE [Kopi av ROYALS.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT aka: William Henry, Duke of Gloucester
0 @N6000000005598973608@ NOTE he was also Duke of Strathearn, Earl of Dublin, and Admiral of the White
1 CONT
1 CONT Prince Henry Frederick, Duke of Cumberland and Strathearn From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT His Royal Highness Prince Henry Frederick, Duke of Cumberland and Strathearn (November 27, 1745 - September 18, 1790) was the sixth child of Frederick, Prince of Wales and Augusta of Saxe-Gotha, and a younger brother of King Georg
1 CONC e III.
1 CONT
1 CONT On March 4, 1767 the Duke of Cumberland allegedly married Olive Wilmot (later Mrs Payne), a commoner, in a secret ceremony. There reportedly was one child, Olivia Wilmot (1772-1834) from this relationship, though the duke's parent
1 CONC hood was never proven. A landscape painter and novelist, Olivia Wilmot married John Thomas Serres, 1759-1825, and later, controversially, assumed the style of Princess Olivia of Cumberland.
1 CONT
1 CONT The Duke's marriage to the commoner Lady Anne Horton (or Houghton) (1743-1808) on October 2, 1771 was the catalyst for the Royal Marriages Act 1772, which forbids any descendant of George II to marry without the monarch's permissi
1 CONC on. There were no children from this marriage. Lady Anne, though from a good family -- she was a daughter of Simon Luttrell, Earl of Carhampton, and the widow of Christopher Horton of Catton Hall -- seems to have been rather loose
1 CONC  with her favors, given one wag's comment that she was "the Duke of Grafton's Mrs Houghton, the Duke of Dorset's Mrs Houghton, everyone's Mrs Houghton."
0 @N6000000002322291984@ NOTE She married her cousin, Christian, in 1766, but he was insane. Her liasian
